            <ArticleTitle>Fatal neutropenic enterocolitis due to clostridium septicum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>594-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of Clostridium septicum enterocolitis in a patient with pre-B acute lymphoblastic leukaemia undergoing autologous stem cell transplant. In the setting of neutropenia, Clostridium septicum should be suspected in patients who develop signs and symptoms of acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
